Too true.=A0 A fuss-budget would insist that there needs to be a notice of =
change of salience to make a move of this sort.=A0 It might, of course, be =
tone of voice in spoken usage, but in written it needs to be something more=
 (or maybe less).=A0 So, we have {bi'u} for the second {lo gerku}, or we ma=
rk the second sentence as a generalization,=A0 so the reference more or les=
s automatically shifts to the supremum.=A0 I think it is generally more lik=
ely that using {lo greku} again so soon -- rather than an anaphoric pronoun=
 or a sentence join -- signals that something other than simple continuatio=
n is going on.=A0 That is part of the reason that the earlier examples in t=
his thread seemed so difficult. they were unnatural in their intended meani=
ng.



